<title>USA: Williams Cos Inc Q3 shr increases.</title>
<headline>Williams Cos Inc Q3 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>TULSA, Okla. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.63		    $0.58</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.63		     0.58</p>
<p> Net			 71,000		   68,500</p>
<p> Revs		     842,200		  712,400</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     108,275		  105,507</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     112,311		  109,587</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$2.30		   $12.24</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 2.27		    11.99</p>
<p> Net			256,300		1,240,700</p>
<p> Revs		   2,573,400		2,018,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     108,094		  100,373</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     112,126		  102,730</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - First Call mean estimate for Q3 was $0.54 per share.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 results were increased by about $6 million from the effect of state income tax adjustments related to 1995. Last year's Q3 was increased by about $14 million,  </p>
<p>representing the after-tax effect of adjustments to certain liability accruals.</p>
<p>The year-to-date 1995 results include an after-tax gain on the sale of network services operations of $1 billion, or $9.79 per share, which is reported as income from discontinued operations.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
